{"name":"Esprit","hex":"#bebd99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"esprit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spirit, enthusiasm.","A wit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/esprit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spirit (animating force)","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and philosophy, spirit is the vital principle or animating essence within humans or, in some views, all living things. Although views of spirit vary between different belief systems, when spirit is contrasted with the soul, the former is often seen as a basic natural force, principle or substance, whereas the latter is used to describe the organized structure of an individual being's consciousness, in humans to include their personality. Spirit as a substance may also be contrasted with matter, where it is usually seen as more subtle, an idea put forth for example in the Principia Mathematica."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_(animating_force)","wikidata":"Q120312205"},{"title":"Enthusiasm","blocks":[{"text":"In modern usage, \"enthusiasm\" refers to intense enjoyment, interest, or approval expressed by a person. The term is allegedly related to playfulness, inventiveness, optimism, zest, verve, and high energy.\nPeople can often characterise the modern version of enthusiasm as \"infectious\" or \"contagious\",\nand sometimes even more metaphorically as a virus in its own right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/EnthusiasticBillyMurray.jpg/330px-EnthusiasticBillyMurray.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enthusiasm","wikidata":"Q840407"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Camp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Camp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Camp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Camp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Camp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Camp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Methodist preachers have been known for their enthusiasm in promulgating the doctrines of the new birth and entire sanctification to the public at events such as tent revivals and camp meetings, which they believe is the reason that God raised them up into existence.[5]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamp_meeting_of_the_Methodists_in_N._America_J._Milbert_del_M._Dubourg_sculp_(cropped).jpg"}],"sounds":{"esprit":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-esprit.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-esprit.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-esprit.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-esprit.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-esprit.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"1995 UAZ 2206 beige rear","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/1995_UAZ_2206_beige_rear.jpg/500px-1995_UAZ_2206_beige_rear.jpg","ratio":1.2959381044487428,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1995_UAZ_2206_beige_rear.jpg","share":0.1925},{"t